      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T14:39:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@Shai, thanks for the code suggestions! I haven\u0027t forgotten about them, but will  leave them pending for now as it\u0027s not entirely clear whether the name-\u003eindices map will live in the Java code as in this CL, or be moved elsewhere.",
      "revId": "2b30583f9aaf9795612db23d6d36056d85ae2c4e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b34e5d3f_623b1bff",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1757736
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T14:39:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think putting the cache in JNI would be okay; I don\u0027t have a preference between implementing the cache there or in BpfInterfaceMapUpdater. +1 to Ryan\u0027s point about the bulk API only being available on newer kernels.\n\nI don\u0027t have benchmark numbers because I haven\u0027t written/figured out a way to generally test NetworkStats performance, but the bug linked in the CL provides an estimate of how much cheaper the new nativeGetIfindexStat+caching is compared to the current nativeGetIfaceStat calls (~30%).",
      "parentUuid": "4cefe3f5_daf6284f",
      "revId": "2b30583f9aaf9795612db23d6d36056d85ae2c4e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
