      "key": {
        "uuid": "6585979f_07cb9554",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/net/BpfInterfaceMapUpdater.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059977
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T21:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense to also implement the reverse mapping in native code, same as how BpfMap works?\nOr to change BpfMap to have bimap functionality, which will allow for some internal implementation that\u0027s much more efficient. Probably much faster too since you\u0027ll be working with proper ints and not with Integer boxed types and doing tons of pointer-chasing for Java HashMaps.\nThe concurrency might end up being simpler too.\nYour call.",
      "revId": "2b30583f9aaf9795612db23d6d36056d85ae2c4e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
